# A loader of ELF shared libraries for Linux, written in SemanticScript (D-154): what `ffi.open`
# of a library other than the C library does in an executable with no C library. Segments are
# mapped from the file, relocations applied and bound at once, symbols found through DT_GNU_HASH
# or DT_HASH, C imports resolved against the runtime's C library (D-153), and initializers run;
# what it cannot load right (thread-local storage, ifuncs, text relocations) traps saying why.
#
# This module is generated from tools/loader.dsl by tools/build.py.

loader is module
loader purpose "A loader of ELF shared libraries on Linux, for ffi.open in an executable with no C library: segments mapped, relocations applied, symbols found by their hash tables, and C imports resolved against the runtime's C library (D-154)"
loader path loader
loader imports standard.machine
loader imports standard.system
loader imports standard.string
loader imports standard.math
loader imports standard.compare
loader imports standard.convert
loader imports standard.bits
loader imports standard.logic
loader imports standard.test
loader imports kernel
loader imports memory
loader imports heap
loader imports frames
loader imports wide
loader imports clibrary
loader exports openLibrary
loader exports symbolOf
loader exports gnuHash
loader exports elfHash

memoryAccess is capability
memoryAccess purpose "Authority to map a library's segments and write its relocations"
memoryAccess grants use machine.memory none

systemCalls is capability
systemCalls purpose "Authority to open a library's file, map it, and run its initializers"
systemCalls grants use system.calls none

# D-154: `ffi.open` of a library other than the C library, on Linux, maps it as ld.so would: the file found as dlopen
# finds a name (a path when it has a `/`, else each directory of LD_LIBRARY_PATH, the asking library's RUNPATH or
# RPATH with $ORIGIN, and the system's library directories), its PT_LOAD segments mapped from the file at a base the
# kernel picks, RELATIVE, GLOB_DAT, JUMP_SLOT, and 64 (ABS64) relocations applied (DT_RELA, DT_JMPREL, DT_RELR), its
# DT_NEEDED libraries loaded first (the C library and its parts, libc.so.6, libm.so.6, and the like, are the
# runtime's own, D-153), its undefined symbols looked up in it, then its libraries breadth first, then the runtime's
# C library, all bound at once as RTLD_NOW binds them; then DT_INIT and DT_INIT_ARRAY run. What the loader cannot do
# right it refuses with a trap that says why, never loading a library wrongly: thread-local storage (PT_TLS, TLS
# relocations), ifunc (IRELATIVE, STT_GNU_IFUNC), text relocations, DT_REL, and a symbol nothing defines. A file that
# is not an ELF shared object for this machine is notFound, as dlopen's failure is. Loaded libraries stay loaded (a
# library is loaded once, known by its device and inode). On x86_64 the thread pointer is set (arch_prctl) to a block
# whose word at 0x28 is the stack protector's canary, which compiled code reads at %fs:0x28; on AArch64 the canary
# is __stack_chk_guard (D-153), filled from getrandom.
# machine.state bytes 1664 to 1791 belong to this module: 1664 the first loaded library, 1672 the thread block (0
# until set), 1680 the page size (0 until read), 1688 to 1831 a struct stat.
